  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the current best at 0.542 acc, and avgpool > transformer and imagenet_vit_l > resnet50 are established from the 3 completed runs. The one untested variable in this top-performing recipe is the RNA encoder—only scgpt has been tried. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether scgpt's pretrained representations are essential or whether the lighter scvi_n200 VAE encoder can match them. This experiment (config_030) changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 while holding the proven-best image encoder, aggregation, and fusion constant, directly isolating the RNA-encoder contribution. If scvi_n200 matches scgpt, we gain a cheaper encoder for future runs; if it falls well short, we confirm scgpt is critical and can focus remaining budget on fusion or profile-setting variations. Expected cost: scvi_n200 is a smaller model than scgpt, so training should be roughly 20-30% cheaper than config_001's 2.94 GPU hours (~2.0–2.3 GPU hours), making this a high-information, low-cost experiment with 6 runs still remaining."
